<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DAR-BE-094 — gorjana month close, comparison 1 (returns against credit memos and RMAs): the checks that need no
  answer from the team yet: R9, R8, R7, R16, and R4's "nothing left open". R4's amount and R6 wait on a Shopify read.

  R16 "A cancelled exchange leaves nothing open in NetSuite." NetSuite never cancels an exchange RMA (none of 30,123
     exchange RMAs since Sep 1): the OMS cancels the return. So FILE_1 is the returns the OMS cancelled (OMS_RETURNS_GQL
     with onlyCancelledReturns, asked of the OMS by status) and FILE_2 the RMAs still OPEN (NS_OPEN_RMA), keyed by return
     id. A pair is the finding: rule GORJANA_R16_STATUS ("statusId = status") never holds between a cancelled return and an
     open RMA, so every pair is a FIELD_MISMATCH row naming the RMA's status. Any cancelled return counts, not only an
     exchange: an open RMA for a cancelled refund is as wrong. Measured: of 183 exchanges the OMS cancelled Oct 1-22, 2
     have an open RMA (Pending Receipt); none has a memo or replacement order.

  R7 "A Happiness Guarantee claim is booked to the Happiness Guarantee account, 42065." Aditi, 2026-10-22: the "Is HG"
     flag (custbody_hc_close_rma) marks HotWax-sourced Happiness Guarantee returns and AfterShip warranty. One single-
     sided run over every credit memo (NS_CREDIT_MEMO_HG_ACCOUNT, with ACCOUNT_USED(42065)); a flagged memo that posts to
     no 42065 line is the finding. 1-22 Oct: 12,938 flagged memos, 12,916 on 42065, so ~22 findings. A $0 memo posts no
     accounting line to any account (CM7665367, 2026-10-21, an AfterShip return at 0), so the finding also needs an amount
     above zero.

  R8 "Every return reaches NetSuite." OMS returns (OMS_RETURNS_GQL with includeReturnsWithoutShopifyRef, so the OMS's own
     numeric-id Happiness Guarantee and sellable returns are read too) against NetSuite RMAs keyed by the HC return id
     without its "HG-" prefix (NS_RETURN_RMA). A completed or received return with no RMA is a finding; one with no
     order first, because the sync skips every completed return with no order (Cindy's workbook: code fix). Requested
     returns are not judged: an RMA is made when HotWax syncs the return, not when the shopper asks. Measured 6-12 Oct:
     of the OMS's numeric returns, 1,439 completed ones are in NetSuite under "HG-<id>" and 94 completed are not (91
     with no channel, 3 Happiness Guarantee). Aditi, 2026-10-22: they should be in NetSuite.

  R4 "Every refund we give a customer is booked in NetSuite at the same amount, to the cent, with nothing left open."
     The "nothing left open" half, as Aditi set it on 2026-10-22: "there should never be an open credit memo", and Darpan
     does nothing in NetSuite about it (it lists the memo; Gorjana Accounting decides). One single-sided run over EVERY
     credit memo in the window (NS_CREDIT_MEMO_STATUS), so an applied one is examined and its finding closes; the
     conclusion CONC_MEMO_LEFT_OPEN takes the memos whose status is Open. 1-22 Oct 2026: about 1,760 open (AfterShip
     returns 1,051, Happiness Guarantee 276, POS 222, warranty channels ~200). Aditi 2026-10-23: "credit memos open with
     unapplied balance up to $5 is ignored", so the conclusion also needs more than $5 unapplied. The unapplied balance is
     transaction.foreignpaymentamountunused (total less applied; foreignamountremaining fails the whole SuiteQL query with
     a 500), read as `unapplied`; the condition is unapplied GT 5, so the finding's evidence shows the amount. A condition,
     not a query filter, so every memo is still read and a finding closes once its balance is applied.

  R9 "Every return carries the customer's full name and the address it came from." (FIRM: name, address; DERIVED: the
     origin address). Two single-sided runs over every RtnAuth and every CustCred in the window
     (tools/netsuite-chain-config/gorjana-month-close-queries.xml, NS_RMA_CUSTOMER / NS_RETURN_CREDIT_CUSTOMER). A
     return's record is one with an HC return id; the address it came from is its shipping address. A conclusion names
     the record with no customer name (BUILTIN.DF of the entity) or no shipping address (the address key only: no
     address text is read or stored).

     Measured on gorjana production, September 2026 (tools/live-probes/NsMonthCloseOrdersProbe.groovy,
     returnsCustomerColumns / returnsCustomerSplits, 2026-10-21):
       RtnAuth with an HC return id    29,090: customer with no name 0, no shipping address 34, no billing address 146
       CustCred with an HC return id   28,673: customer with no name 0, no shipping address 0, no BILLING address 17,625
     The billing address IS tested since 2026-10-22 (Aditi: "billing is required too"): CONC_NO_BILLING_ADDRESS, after
     the name and the return address (a record takes its first matching conclusion). Expect about 17,600 credit memos
     and ~150 RMAs a month at first: 61% of return credits have none, on every channel. Every address that exists has
     text, and no customer on these records lacks a name, so the name rule guards against a regression.

  Every record is read, not only the bad ones, so a fixed one is examined and its finding closes (as for R2).

  automationId is blank on purpose: an automation is created per environment (prod-owed on DAR-BE-094). Like R2's, the
  two automations are data rows with ONE FILE_1 NETSUITE_SUITEQL source naming its query in safeMetadataJson.

  NOT seed data - tenant configuration. Load per install, AFTER AuditSeedData.xml, GorjanaMonthCloseCatalogData.xml and
  tools/netsuite-chain-config/gorjana-month-close-queries.xml (the rule sets name those query rows):

      ec.entity.makeDataLoader().location("component://darpan/data/GorjanaMonthCloseReturnsChecksData.xml").load()
-->
